--- a/mods/ITEMS/mcl_maps/init.lua
+++ b/mods/ITEMS/mcl_maps/init.lua
@@ load_map(): dynamic_add_media's callback only fires once a PLAYER has
+ received the media. With nobody connected (map import / headless
+ server) it never fires, and mcl_itemframes' set_item "dirty recursive
+ hack" then retries update_entity EVERY step -- spawning a NEW frame
+ display entity each time because find_entity cannot see already-saved
+ (static) objects. Observed: one mapblock with 50 map frames ended up
+ with 50,050 mcl_itemframes:item objects (museum import 2026-09-25).
+ Fix: when no player exists to send the media to, mark the map loaded
+ and invoke the callback immediately (the texture is on disk either
+ way; the callback only hands its name to the caller).
+ Applied to ~/dev/mineclonia-git (2026-09-25). RE-APPLY after upstream
+ merges -- without it every map-frame import multiplies entities.
